<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine Jan-Feb GDP falls 8.9 pct year-on-year.</title>
<headline>Ukraine Jan-Feb GDP falls 8.9 pct year-on-year.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ukrainian gross domestic product in the first two months of this year was 12.03 billion hryvnias, 8.9 percent lower than a year earlier, the Statistics Ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>    UKRAINE GDP		 Jan-Feb 97  Jan 97   Jan-Feb 96</p>
<p>    year-on-year pct change -8.9	  -10.4    -11.5</p>
<p>Prime Minister Pavlo Lazarenko has forecast that GDP will grow this year by 0.5 to 1.0 percent, the first growth since independence in 1991. GDP fell 10.0 percent in 1996.</p>
<p>--Kiev Newsroom, +380 44 229 2264</p>
